From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:34:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] scheduler v2: analytic scorer, lazy planner, learning and
 summary

The scheduler now ranks (P, S) by the existence study's analytic model
(--model analytic, the default) instead of the fitted regression, which
has no growth beyond N ~ 5.5k, under-predicts diagonals ~2.3x and only
sees non-increasing exponents:

* Pool + ProfileStore: the wide pool (pool.py), each P's model profile on
  24 grid sums computed once by niced worker processes into a float16
  memmap (resumable), P outside the pool in extra.json.
* AnalyticScorer: magic squares per CPU-second per sum from the profile,
  the learned class factors per calibration cell (N' band x k x ratio x
  x band), per-P gamma factors and the label-aware time law; units as in
  v1 (unit time, drop rule, covered gaps), node and time limits per unit.
* Planner: lazy greedy over a heap keyed by 1.1 x the best grid density at
  or after each P's frontier, so the 378k P need no per-unit scan; the
  frontier starts at ceil(S0) and never calls bin/enumerate.
* Learning: three main-effects Poisson GLMs (MAP, Laplace covariance)
  whose priors reproduce the review factors, per-P gamma factors, and a
  Bayesian-ridge time refit per msearch engine.
* Summary: unit files are parsed incrementally (byte offsets, .gz read)
  into per-P coverage, counts and per-cell expectations, time and bias
  statistics, and notable squares, so state stays bounded at CPU-years.
* report (calibration tables, time and N/label bias, fresh vs repeat
  units from launched_6.jsonl), forecast (planner simulation, composition,
  posterior band), profile, pool --stats and compact commands.

--model regression --pool classic keeps v1's behaviour.

